1
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,960
When you were locked up,

2
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:36,920
<i>was there anyone else down there?</i>

3
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,960
<i>I don't know what you're planning,</i>

4
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,200
<i>but you shouldn't go down there.</i>

5
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,800
Koh.

6
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:46,000
We know you came to Poipet
looking for your dad.

7
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,560
Koh's been captured.

8
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:49,160
<i>We're figuring out a way to get inside.</i>

9
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,720
There are way too many of them.

10
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:52,800
How are they supposed to get out?

11
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:56,200
<i>Can you tell Mungkorn to wait until</i>
<i>tonight? It'll be safer to escape then.</i>

12
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,000
<i>No, Chen.</i>

13
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,120
<i>If we wait that long,</i>
<i>my friends won't make it.</i>

14
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,760
<i>Found them. All of them.</i>

15
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,000
Then, let's do this.

16
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,600
Three, two, one.

17
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,960
Damn it! A bomb!

18
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,200
You thought I'd die that easily? Dream on!

19
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,480
Risa!

20
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,360
Hang in there.

21
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,640
Chen, this way!

22
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,160
Over here!

23
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,840
-Hurry!
-Come on, sis.

24
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,920
-Open the door!
-Easy, that hurts!

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,360
Slow down.

26
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:27,720
Sis, get in and wait inside.

27
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,560
-Okay.
-Chen, what happened?

28
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,520
That guy didn't die.

29
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,360
And he came back with a whole crew.

30
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:36,040
What? He's still alive?

31
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,960
Then I didn't kill anyone. Thank Buddha.

32
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,320
-Angpao!
-Yeah?

33
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,360
We didn't kill him,
but he's about to kill us.

34
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:51,240
Help me look.
Is there a gun in here? Hurry!

35
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,480
I'm going back to help them.

36
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:56,480
-No.
-Ask over the radio what weapons we have.

37
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,080
Uncle, can you hear me?

38
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:00,360
-Yeah, go ahead.
-Do we have another gun in the car?

39
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:02,520
No. We're out of guns.

40
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:05,640
Then what do we have
that can be used as a weapon?

41
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:07,080
A weapon?

42
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,560
Will this work?

43
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:14,840
Hey, Chen.

44
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,720
What is it?

45
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,640
Uncle.

46
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,640
Get out now! More backup is coming!

47
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,720
Yak.

48
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,480
They're swarming the place. What do we do?

49
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,880
Bro, let's do this. Give me the gun.

50
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:36,320
You go help them outside
and take Mungkorn with you.

51
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,200
I'll go help Risa.

52
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,360
-Watch yourself.
-Yak.

53
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,680
-Huh?
-Hong's outside. Go, now!

54
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,360
-Go!
-Hurry!

55
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:44,520
Go! Now!

56
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:45,680
-Move!
-Hurry!

57
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,880
Risa, get ready.

58
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,120
Move! Now!

59
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:17,160
Risa!

60
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:20,040
Take it easy, bro and boy.

61
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,279
Hurry!

62
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,720
-Mungkorn. Are you okay?
-Mung!

63
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,760
Mungkorn.

64
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:25,240
-There's blood!
-Bro.

65
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,520
-Mungkorn.
-Open it.

66
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,760
-Calm down.
-Don't ask questions right now.

67
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:29,800
-Where are they?
-Over there, Uncle.

68
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,000
Koh.

69
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:35,640
Just wait.

70
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:38,240
I brought you two bombs.

71
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:43,200
Yak, is this really the time for jokes?
Those are fake grenades.

72
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,160
Who said they're fake?

73
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,560
This time, they're real.

74
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:57,240
Yak, get down! Everybody, take cover!

75
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,520
Over there!

76
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,000
Sis, watch out! Mungkorn, look out!

77
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,320
Out of bullets, Koh?

78
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:46,800
Time to die, you servant's son.

79
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,760
Who the hell did that?

80
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,640
You little brat,
what do you think you're doing?

81
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,160
This is what I'm doing.

82
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:42,440
Oab!

83
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:53,440
I changed my mind.
I'm escaping with you guys.

84
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,880
That stun won't keep them down
for long. Let's go. Hurry.

85
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,280
Koh!

86
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:11,920
Koh!

87
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,040
Wait. Where do you think you're going?

88
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:14,840
I'm going to help my friends.

89
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,240
Are you crazy?
If you run out there, you're dead.

90
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:20,600
What now?

91
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:23,400
We're already about to die,
and now there's another one?

92
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:27,360
I've got one more for you.
You wanna eat this?

93
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,720
Hurry, Yak!

94
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:30,560
Take it. Eat this!

95
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:36,840
Move! Hurry!

96
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,120
Bro, get everyone out of here.

97
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,360
Koh, but…

98
00:07:58,440 --> 00:07:59,560
Don't worry about us.

99
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:02,320
If we stay here, we're all dead. Go. Now.

100
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:08,080
Go around the building
and head into the forest. Move!

101
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,200
Now!

102
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,640
Go!

103
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,720
-Move!
-Get in!

104
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,120
-Go! Get in the car!
-Koh!

105
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:20,160
-Get in now!
-Hurry!

106
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:22,880
After them! Move!

107
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,800
-Get in! Now!
-Hurry!

108
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,960
-Hurry!
-Hong, get in!

109
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,240
Gao, hurry. Let's go.

110
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:30,440
Get in the car!

111
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:50,680
Mungkorn.

112
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:53,160
Hang in there. Stay awake.

113
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,560
Are we gonna make it out alive?

114
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:57,720
Hey, don't worry.

115
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,280
As long as Yak's driving, we'll be fine.

116
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,040
Wait.

117
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,520
We're on foot,

118
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,600
and they're in vehicles.
We're not getting away like this.

119
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:19,280
We can if we take a route
their vehicles can't follow.

120
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:21,320
But this is open forest.

121
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:24,640
Even if we climb a tree,
they'll just shoot us down.

122
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,520
Quiet, sis.

123
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:28,800
What is it?

124
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,440
I think I hear running water.

125
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:34,280
-Which way?
-This way.

126
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,880
Let's go. Hurry.

127
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:45,120
-Where the hell did they go?
-Hey.

128
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,560
-Go back and check again.
-Got it.

129
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,320
Come on.

130
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:02,040
See, kid?

131
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:04,000
I told you we'd make it.

132
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,000
Let's go back and help Koh and Risa.

133
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,600
Have you lost your mind?

134
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,440
We barely made it out alive.

135
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:14,520
But if we don't go back,
they might get killed.

136
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,000
Mungkorn! Wake up!

137
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,640
Mungkorn!

138
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,960
Don't fall asleep! Mungkorn!

139
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:23,400
-Hey.
-Wake up!

140
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,360
-Someone help me!
-Mung!

141
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,840
Wait.

142
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,600
Looks like the pain
is starting to hit him.

143
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:30,760
The bullet's still inside.
We can't remove it here.

144
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,240
Let's go to a hospital.

145
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:35,200
No. We can't.
If we go now, we'll all get arrested.

146
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:36,680
Then let them arrest us.

147
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:38,200
I'm not letting my friend die here.

148
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,680
-Yeah.
-Hey, Mung!

149
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:42,760
-Hey, don't fall asleep!
-Mung!

150
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,000
What do we do?

151
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,600
We have to cross.
Their vehicles can't follow us there.

152
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:04,640
I don't need help. I can walk.

153
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:10,760
Careful.

154
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:41,120
Can you move faster?
They're catching up. Go!

155
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,040
Oab!

156
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,920
Are you okay, Oab?

157
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,720
I think my foot's stuck.

158
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,320
-It hurts!
-Does it hurt?

159
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:12,280
You guys should go.
I'll take care of myself.

160
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,440
No. I'm not leaving you behind.

161
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:27,960
What are you doing?

162
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:34,080
They have to be around here somewhere.

163
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:37,680
Keep searching. If you don't find them,
don't come back.

164
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:39,760
Find a place to hide.

165
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,720
Get down. Now!

166
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:07,880
Get down. Hurry.

167
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:29,240
Move.

168
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:30,280
Bro.

169
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,960
-Where should we put him?
-Careful.

170
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,000
-Put him on the couch.
-Hold him for a second.

171
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:35,800
Lay him down gently.

172
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:37,920
-Come here.
-Easy.

173
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:40,000
How are you feeling?

174
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:42,800
He's lost a lot of blood.

175
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:45,720
-What do we do now?
-Go check if they're still following us.

176
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,320
-Yes.
-Hey.

177
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,360
-Get some hot water ready.
-I'm on it.

178
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,520
I'm back.

179
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:07,680
I got cotton, gauze, and alcohol.

180
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:10,600
Angpao, do you know how to clean a wound?

181
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:12,040
I think I can manage.

182
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,040
Uncle, you can do this, right?

183
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:18,120
Pulling out a bullet
isn't much different from picking a lock.

184
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,360
Let's do it.

185
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,960
His pulse is still strong.

186
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:25,720
Mung. Stay with me.

187
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,800
I'll clean the wound.

188
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,040
-Uncle, move aside.
-Okay.

189
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,520
That hurts!

190
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,640
Can't you be gentler?

191
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:49,920
Mr. Louis has arrived.
He requests to see you downstairs.

192
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,120
You're pretty late, Mr. Louis.

193
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:47,520
So this was your plan?

194
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,120
Lure them all together

195
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,880
and let them tear down my building?

196
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,600
And you still let them get away?

197
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:57,520
Don't worry.

198
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,720
I've already sent my men after them.

199
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,600
This is on you.

200
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:09,160
You'll be the one hunting them down.

201
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,360
I'm still injured.

202
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,160
Even if you're on your last breath,

203
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,120
you do

204
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,720
what I tell you.

205
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,320
I'll be waiting for good news.

206
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,400
Let's stop here for tonight.

207
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,320
Okay.

208
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,320
Get down.

209
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:59,920
-Does it hurt a lot?
-Yes.

210
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,600
-Go sit over there.
-Sit down first.

211
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:02,800
-Slowly.
-Take it easy.

212
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:04,839
Sit down slowly.

213
00:17:23,319 --> 00:17:24,160
What are you doing?

214
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,680
Her ankle's probably sprained.

215
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,480
Sorry.

216
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:59,720
I'm going to wrap it
so you don't move it too much.

217
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:06,560
Let's sit lower. Come on.

218
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,880
Slowly.

219
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,920
Try bending this knee a little.

220
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:12,600
Easy.

221
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:20,080
You'll be alright soon. Trust me.

222
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,600
You can get some sleep if you want.
I'll keep watch.

223
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,760
Okay.

224
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:21,560
Our little vacation is…

225
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:25,880
totally ruined, Yak.

226
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:28,680
Next time,
let's go somewhere farther away.

227
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:31,560
Seriously. Can we even trust that?

228
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:35,000
We came all this way
and still got dragged into trouble.

229
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:37,840
Next trip, I'm picking the country.

230
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,880
Macau or Malaysia?

231
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,520
Macau or Malaysia?
Are you even listening to me?

232
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:47,120
I said I'm picking the country.

233
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,200
Okay. Macau.

234
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:51,480
-Malaysia.
-Why Malaysia?

235
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:52,400
I want to eat murtabak.

236
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,400
Here.

237
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:01,640
I bought this for you.

238
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:12,440
Thanks, Hong.

239
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:21,840
Thank you for coming back to help me.

240
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:25,760
We only came back
because Angpao asked us to.

241
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,240
Hey. Are you still mad at me?

242
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:38,560
Yak, I've decided where we're going.

243
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,800
Macau, right?

244
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:41,640
Malaysia.

245
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,880
Go pack your things.

246
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:48,840
-I said pack your things.
-What the hell, Gao?

247
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,360
I'm not letting you drink that.

248
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:11,600
Hong.

249
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,560
You're sick right now,

250
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:14,840
and you're still drinking beer?

251
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,480
Do you want to die young or something?

252
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:19,400
I'm going to die anyway. Give it back.

253
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:21,880
-No. I'm not letting you.
-Hey! I said give it back.

254
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:23,640
-Give it back!
-I'm not letting you drink.

255
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:24,880
Hey, give it back!

256
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:30,320
Hey. Why are you guys taking my beer?

257
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,320
You have cancer, don't you?

258
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:40,480
Aren't you afraid of dying
if you keep drinking?

259
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:41,800
I'm going to die anyway.

260
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,560
Why do you care now?

261
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:47,200
Just let me do what I want.

262
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:50,000
So I can get it over with

263
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:52,200
and leave this world sooner.

264
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:59,560
We never wanted you to die.

265
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:01,680
Don't you get that?

266
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:08,680
We don't care about the money.

267
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:10,840
You matter more than any of it.

268
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,760
We're upset

269
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:17,680
because you never told us you were sick.

270
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:21,160
We had to hear it from someone else.

271
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:25,840
I was scared.

272
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:36,320
I was scared

273
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:39,800
that if I told you,
everything would change.

274
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:45,400
I didn't want to see you both sad.

275
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:51,320
I just want to enjoy my life with you guys

276
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:53,400
one last time before I die.

277
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:55,480
That's all.

278
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:07,840
I love you, Hong.

279
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:11,120
You're going to be okay.

280
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:37,840
Hong, you're not allowed to die.

281
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:40,720
You hear me? You're not allowed.

282
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:02,400
Oh, you're awake?

283
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:14,200
When did you take that?

284
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:17,000
Last night, you dropped it
when you fell asleep.

285
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,160
So I borrowed it.

286
00:24:21,040 --> 00:24:21,840
What are you doing?

287
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:27,320
I'm making her a walking stick

288
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,800
so she can support herself.

289
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:30,840
We still have a long way to go today.

290
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:33,120
I can't carry her all day.

291
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:35,200
Or are you going to carry her?

292
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:36,600
You sure?

293
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:39,560
Your arms and legs
are so thin, like chopsticks,

294
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:41,080
and you're tiny as a puppy.

295
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:44,560
I'm roasting you,
and you're just sitting there taking it?

296
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:48,680
I'm standing right now.
Who's as tall as a giant like you?

297
00:24:52,440 --> 00:24:53,960
Anyway, it's good you're awake.

298
00:24:58,640 --> 00:24:59,760
I've got something to show you.

299
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:00,720
What is it?

300
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:01,960
Follow me.

301
00:25:03,960 --> 00:25:05,320
Come on.

302
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:13,280
Are we really going
to leave Oab there alone?

303
00:25:13,360 --> 00:25:14,720
Yeah.

304
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:16,960
Let her rest a little longer.

305
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:19,440
So where are you taking me?

306
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,320
We're here.

307
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:25,640
What is it?

308
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,240
There.

309
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:31,280
That means someone's
been here setting traps.

310
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:33,080
So?

311
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:35,240
That means there are people around.

312
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:38,600
They can help us get out of this forest
and contact Chen.

313
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:46,880
-What are you doing?
-What?

314
00:25:46,960 --> 00:25:49,040
I'm going to see
if there are any fish in there.

315
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:53,600
We haven't eaten all night.

316
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:54,880
I'm hungry.

317
00:25:56,240 --> 00:25:57,120
Wait.

318
00:25:57,960 --> 00:26:00,320
This waterfall is slippery.
If you get hurt too,

319
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:01,640
I won't be able to handle it.

320
00:26:01,720 --> 00:26:03,360
Hey, Risa!

321
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:12,280
What are you laughing at?

322
00:26:12,360 --> 00:26:14,560
You're just so clumsy.

323
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:30,160
I'm not dumb enough
to let you pull me in and get wet too.

324
00:26:31,360 --> 00:26:32,280
Oh yeah?

325
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:34,160
You think you're clever, huh?

326
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:43,120
I'm completely soaked.

327
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:32,360
What are you doing? You'll alert them.

328
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:34,240
I saw someone running that way, sir.

329
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:50,480
Oab! Are you okay?

330
00:27:50,560 --> 00:27:52,360
-Are you alright?
-They're coming this way.

331
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:54,520
Get on my back! Hurry!

332
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:25,040
Pao.

333
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:28,560
Mung!

334
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:30,440
You're awake?

335
00:28:36,040 --> 00:28:37,560
Mungkorn, how are you feeling?

336
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:39,280
Where am I?

337
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:41,520
We brought you here to recover

338
00:28:41,600 --> 00:28:42,960
at Gao and Phayak's place.

339
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:45,200
Where's Risa?

340
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:51,440
Wait.

341
00:28:51,520 --> 00:28:52,840
Calm down. Where are you going?

342
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:55,640
We have to go save Risa.

343
00:28:56,280 --> 00:28:58,080
But you're not fully recovered yet.

344
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:04,000
They've tracked us to the guesthouse.

345
00:29:04,080 --> 00:29:05,440
Seriously?

346
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:19,120
Hurry!

347
00:29:22,080 --> 00:29:22,840
Go!

348
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:31,120
Boss!

349
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:33,640
Go after them!

350
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:39,560
Can you walk any faster?

351
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:41,560
They're going to catch us at this rate.

352
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:43,200
What do you want me to do?

353
00:29:44,200 --> 00:29:45,040
Let's do this.

354
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:49,600
You take cover. Take Oab with you.

355
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:51,080
What about you?

356
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:52,640
I'll lure them away.

357
00:29:53,520 --> 00:29:54,440
Find somewhere to hide.

358
00:29:54,520 --> 00:29:56,680
Are you crazy?

359
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,080
Go! After him!

360
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:13,400
Hurry!

361
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:50,240
They're around here. Split up and search.

362
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:52,720
You two go that way. You come with me.

363
00:30:52,800 --> 00:30:54,080
Yes, sir.

364
00:31:56,720 --> 00:31:58,960
Don't move, or he dies.

365
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:09,080
Damn it.

366
00:32:24,680 --> 00:32:27,000
You're out of bullets again, Koh.

367
00:33:09,640 --> 00:33:11,040
So what now, Koh?

368
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:14,400
Think fast.

369
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:17,920
What are you going to do? Fight me?

370
00:33:19,840 --> 00:33:20,600
Jump off the cliff?

371
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:24,080
But don't jump.

372
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,680
You might actually survive.

373
00:33:27,720 --> 00:33:30,560
I'd rather kill you. That's a sure thing.

374
00:33:38,160 --> 00:33:41,600
Die, you servant's son.

375
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:08,679
Go to hell, Koh!

376
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:25,960
Koh!

377
00:35:14,120 --> 00:35:15,320
You want to die, huh?

378
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:36,480
Someone like you can't kill me.

379
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:42,560
I can.

380
00:35:43,720 --> 00:35:46,200
Koh!

381
00:35:49,200 --> 00:35:50,040
Don't!

382
00:35:50,960 --> 00:35:52,080
No!

383
00:36:13,840 --> 00:36:14,600
Let's go.

384
00:36:22,640 --> 00:36:23,520
Let's go.

385
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:38,880
Why are you making so much noise?

386
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:42,120
If we're sending signals in the forest,
we should use animal sounds.

387
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:44,640
Everyone.

388
00:36:44,720 --> 00:36:48,120
There's still no sign of Koh and Risa.

389
00:36:49,240 --> 00:36:51,040
And they haven't contacted us.

390
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:53,400
Should we go deeper into the forest?

391
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:54,640
We can't do that.

392
00:36:54,720 --> 00:36:57,280
Even though we escaped them,

393
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:59,440
we don't know
if they're still following us.

394
00:36:59,520 --> 00:37:02,480
Maybe we should find somewhere quiet
and lay low first.

395
00:37:02,560 --> 00:37:04,320
Wait until they stop searching for us,

396
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:06,240
then go look for Risa.

397
00:37:06,320 --> 00:37:08,000
But I'm worried it'll be too late.

398
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:10,240
Hey, don't forget.

399
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:12,680
They've sent people to look for Koh too.

400
00:37:12,760 --> 00:37:15,880
If we rush in blindly and run into them,

401
00:37:15,960 --> 00:37:19,600
it'll be a disaster.
We've got nothing, no guns, no explosives.

402
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:23,240
-Everyone.
-Hurry up.

403
00:37:23,320 --> 00:37:24,760
-They're here again.
-Open the door.

404
00:37:24,840 --> 00:37:26,520
-Quick, bro!
-Watch out.

405
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:28,520
-Hong, watch out.
-Hurry, this way.

406
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:29,920
-Slowly.
-Take cover!

407
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:36,320
It's coming this way.

408
00:37:36,960 --> 00:37:38,800
What the hell?

409
00:37:54,040 --> 00:37:55,200
It's heading straight for us.

410
00:37:55,720 --> 00:37:57,320
We're not going to make it.

411
00:38:05,320 --> 00:38:06,400
I surrender.

412
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:07,920
Please spare us. I surrender.

413
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:10,160
We surrender. Don't shoot.

414
00:38:10,240 --> 00:38:11,160
Don't shoot us.

415
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:15,120
Hello, everyone.

416
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:45,040
Are you still thinking about it?

417
00:38:53,200 --> 00:38:54,200
Don't overthink it.

418
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:57,200
If you hadn't done that,

419
00:38:58,640 --> 00:39:00,040
we might all be dead by now.

420
00:39:08,640 --> 00:39:10,160
Thank you for saving my life.

421
00:39:29,840 --> 00:39:31,760
Let me take a look at your ankle.

422
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:34,320
Sorry.

423
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:40,280
It doesn't hurt anymore.
Koh, you're amazing.

424
00:39:41,720 --> 00:39:45,200
But you still need to keep it wrapped
and use the crutch.

425
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:46,600
So you don't injure it again, okay?

426
00:39:47,520 --> 00:39:48,280
Yes, Doctor.

427
00:39:49,360 --> 00:39:52,560
Right now, my foot is itching like crazy.

428
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:54,680
Can I take the wrap off,
scratch it, and then put it back on?

429
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:56,600
You're feeling better
and already acting up again.

430
00:39:58,960 --> 00:40:00,560
You touched my foot,
and now you're touching my head?

431
00:40:00,640 --> 00:40:03,320
Don't tease me
just because you're shy around Risa.

432
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:05,200
Hey, I'm not shy!

433
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:13,960
Hey, Oab. I'm curious.

434
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:17,280
When I told you to run away
with me earlier,

435
00:40:17,360 --> 00:40:19,560
why didn't you come?

436
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:25,320
Didn't you want to go back to your dad?

437
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:36,880
Actually, my home is around here.

438
00:40:39,040 --> 00:40:40,840
I thought you were Thai.

439
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:43,840
I am Thai. I'm from Sa Kaeo.

440
00:40:43,920 --> 00:40:46,960
The fish you caught earlier

441
00:40:47,040 --> 00:40:49,040
could've been from my dad's trap.

442
00:40:49,120 --> 00:40:51,680
But when he got into debt,

443
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:54,880
we had to flee and stay
on this side of the border.

444
00:40:55,680 --> 00:40:58,840
When you said you had to work

445
00:40:58,920 --> 00:41:00,920
at the call center because of your dad…

446
00:41:02,560 --> 00:41:03,520
Yeah.

447
00:41:04,640 --> 00:41:06,480
There's no age limit for that job.

448
00:41:07,120 --> 00:41:08,880
He saw an ad online.

449
00:41:09,520 --> 00:41:11,960
Since I knew how to use
the internet and computers,

450
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:14,520
he signed me up.

451
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:16,680
At first,

452
00:41:17,320 --> 00:41:19,560
I didn't even know
what kind of job it was.

453
00:41:19,640 --> 00:41:20,360
What?

454
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:23,080
But once you found out it was illegal,

455
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:25,000
why did he make you keep doing it?

456
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:27,480
Because it makes money.

457
00:41:28,160 --> 00:41:29,680
I knew it was wrong.

458
00:41:30,360 --> 00:41:31,800
But what else could I do?

459
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:35,400
Poor people don't have many choices.

460
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:04,840
Stop right there!

461
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:07,200
Who are you?

462
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:12,560
Bring me to your boss.

463
00:42:21,480 --> 00:42:24,120
Why are you bringing this to me?

464
00:42:24,840 --> 00:42:26,000
Let's just say

465
00:42:26,840 --> 00:42:28,640
I have a personal grudge against them.

466
00:42:32,200 --> 00:42:34,840
How can I trust

467
00:42:36,160 --> 00:42:38,080
you're not with them?

468
00:42:42,080 --> 00:42:45,200
I'll bring you their bodies to prove it.

469
00:42:47,240 --> 00:42:49,200
Mr. Louis, we've got a problem.

470
00:42:50,280 --> 00:42:51,560
What is it?

471
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:54,680
Someone tipped off the Thai authorities
about our call center operation.

472
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:57,080
Thai police are crossing
the border right now.

473
00:43:01,200 --> 00:43:03,480
Destroy all the evidence. Now.

474
00:43:03,560 --> 00:43:04,760
Yes, Mr. Louis.

475
00:43:11,800 --> 00:43:15,400
If you take them all down,
I'll pay you a million baht per head.

476
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:21,320
Gladly.

477
00:43:38,840 --> 00:43:40,040
Is this your house?

478
00:43:40,560 --> 00:43:41,520
Yes.

479
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:45,680
Dad.

480
00:43:57,600 --> 00:43:59,120
Wait for me here.

481
00:44:00,240 --> 00:44:01,440
Dad.

482
00:44:03,440 --> 00:44:04,280
Dad.

483
00:44:04,920 --> 00:44:06,360
No wonder she's so familiar

484
00:44:06,440 --> 00:44:07,680
-with this forest.
-Dad!

485
00:44:07,760 --> 00:44:09,120
Yeah.

486
00:44:20,640 --> 00:44:22,760
You're the ones who stole my fish.

487
00:44:22,840 --> 00:44:24,400
Please calm down.

488
00:44:24,480 --> 00:44:26,520
-What?
-Dad!

489
00:44:31,920 --> 00:44:32,880
Oab.

490
00:44:34,160 --> 00:44:35,040
Oab.

491
00:44:36,760 --> 00:44:37,760
Dad.

492
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:39,200
Oab. How did you get here?

493
00:44:40,160 --> 00:44:42,120
Oab.

494
00:44:51,840 --> 00:44:54,200
Koh. You're safe, right?

495
00:44:54,280 --> 00:44:56,840
Yeah, we're safe.

496
00:44:57,400 --> 00:44:58,360
<i>Yes!</i>

497
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:03,000
Everyone, I've got Koh
and Risa on the line.

498
00:45:03,080 --> 00:45:04,760
They're safe.

499
00:45:06,080 --> 00:45:08,040
Chen, can I talk to them? Koh.

500
00:45:08,120 --> 00:45:09,560
Is Risa okay?

501
00:45:11,120 --> 00:45:14,080
She's fine. We're at Oab's house.

502
00:45:14,640 --> 00:45:15,800
The girl Risa helped earlier.

503
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:17,800
Then send us your location.

504
00:45:17,880 --> 00:45:19,160
We'll come get you right away.

505
00:45:20,280 --> 00:45:22,560
Koh, I want to talk to Risa.

506
00:45:26,160 --> 00:45:27,680
She doesn't seem to be around here.

507
00:45:32,920 --> 00:45:33,840
Oab.

508
00:45:35,760 --> 00:45:37,080
I'm sorry.

509
00:45:38,800 --> 00:45:40,320
It's okay, Dad.

510
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:43,720
At least I made it out.

511
00:45:44,520 --> 00:45:45,840
I never thought

512
00:45:47,080 --> 00:45:48,600
you'd have to go through all this.

513
00:45:54,960 --> 00:45:57,840
Thank you so much for bringing her out.

514
00:45:59,360 --> 00:46:00,360
Yes.

515
00:46:04,960 --> 00:46:06,320
But may I say something?

516
00:46:08,880 --> 00:46:10,520
Don't let yourself believe

517
00:46:11,040 --> 00:46:13,880
that being poor means you have no choices.

518
00:46:15,880 --> 00:46:18,720
I know poverty can make life
incredibly difficult.

519
00:46:19,880 --> 00:46:23,400
But I believe we still
get to choose how we fight it.

520
00:46:28,840 --> 00:46:30,840
I'd rather struggle

521
00:46:32,960 --> 00:46:34,480
alongside the people I love

522
00:46:35,280 --> 00:46:37,240
than live comfortably
with no one left beside me.

523
00:46:41,240 --> 00:46:42,680
Because nothing

524
00:46:43,840 --> 00:46:46,120
can replace the happiness

525
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:49,000
of being with your dad

526
00:46:50,320 --> 00:46:51,840
and your family.

527
00:47:02,800 --> 00:47:03,800
Don't cry.

528
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:14,600
There, there.

529
00:47:25,560 --> 00:47:27,600
Why didn't you ever tell me

530
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:29,000
you knew my father?

531
00:47:32,120 --> 00:47:34,040
I didn't want you
getting dragged into this.

532
00:47:36,120 --> 00:47:37,600
But he's my dad.

533
00:47:38,840 --> 00:47:41,280
I have a right to know about him, don't I?

534
00:47:47,760 --> 00:47:50,040
I knew Aek back when I was a cop.

535
00:47:51,720 --> 00:47:54,080
<i>Back then, he worked</i>
<i>for a powerful figure.</i>

536
00:47:54,800 --> 00:47:56,880
<i>I was assigned to collect protection money</i>

537
00:47:56,960 --> 00:47:58,640
<i>from the same places he operated.</i>

538
00:47:58,720 --> 00:48:01,760
That's how we kept crossing paths
and eventually became friends.

539
00:48:03,920 --> 00:48:05,440
Then one day…

540
00:48:07,080 --> 00:48:08,480
<i>He became a target.</i>

541
00:48:10,720 --> 00:48:13,040
<i>I still don't know what he did.</i>

542
00:48:15,640 --> 00:48:17,560
<i>But I was ordered to bring him in.</i>

543
00:48:21,680 --> 00:48:23,720
In the end, I was just bait.

544
00:48:29,720 --> 00:48:31,360
<i>James's men turned on me.</i>

545
00:48:33,360 --> 00:48:34,840
<i>They were going to shoot Aek.</i>

546
00:48:51,720 --> 00:48:53,520
<i>But luckily, he managed to escape.</i>

547
00:48:58,600 --> 00:49:01,360
After that, I was charged
with multiple crimes.

548
00:49:02,520 --> 00:49:03,880
Shooting a police officer,

549
00:49:04,960 --> 00:49:06,520
helping a suspect escape,

550
00:49:08,240 --> 00:49:10,280
and even being framed
in the protection money case.

551
00:49:15,440 --> 00:49:17,520
After that, I never heard from Aek again.

552
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:22,240
At first, I thought he got away safely.

553
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:26,040
Then I found out you're his daughter.

554
00:49:31,400 --> 00:49:34,720
I knew he would never leave
his daughter behind.

555
00:49:37,280 --> 00:49:39,120
That's why I started looking for him.

556
00:49:40,840 --> 00:49:42,720
And I found a lead.

557
00:49:43,640 --> 00:49:44,640
Louis is the only one

558
00:49:46,200 --> 00:49:47,600
who knows where he is.

559
00:49:52,200 --> 00:49:53,240
You…

560
00:49:53,920 --> 00:49:56,040
You know my dad better than I do.

561
00:49:59,800 --> 00:50:01,520
He never told me anything

562
00:50:03,480 --> 00:50:07,400
about his work or who he worked for.

563
00:50:15,240 --> 00:50:18,360
Do you know what my last memory

564
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:20,760
of him is?

565
00:50:23,800 --> 00:50:25,600
I saw him pickpocketing a man

566
00:50:25,680 --> 00:50:27,640
at a train station.

567
00:50:31,440 --> 00:50:32,360
TICKETS

568
00:50:33,160 --> 00:50:34,640
<i>I was so shocked.</i>

569
00:50:35,960 --> 00:50:37,160
<i>Seeing him do that</i>

570
00:50:44,760 --> 00:50:46,720
<i>made me realize</i>

571
00:50:47,240 --> 00:50:48,920
my dad

572
00:50:51,600 --> 00:50:54,240
might not be the good man
I believed he was.

573
00:51:01,280 --> 00:51:02,760
But to me…

574
00:51:05,320 --> 00:51:08,160
he's one of the best people
I've ever known.

575
00:51:45,200 --> 00:51:46,840
I'm sorry, Risa.

576
00:51:50,720 --> 00:51:52,080
If it weren't for me,

577
00:51:54,560 --> 00:51:56,120
your life wouldn't
have turned out like this.

578
00:52:30,280 --> 00:52:31,120
Clear!

579
00:52:38,000 --> 00:52:38,800
Clear!

580
00:52:41,240 --> 00:52:42,440
Help!

581
00:52:42,520 --> 00:52:44,760
Somebody help!

582
00:52:44,840 --> 00:52:46,440
-Help!
-Help!

583
00:52:46,520 --> 00:52:49,960
We've found the victims.
They're being held in basement cells.

584
00:52:51,960 --> 00:52:53,080
We've located the victims.

585
00:52:53,760 --> 00:52:55,760
Everyone is being held in the basement.

586
00:52:58,640 --> 00:52:59,600
Get them out.

587
00:52:59,680 --> 00:53:01,480
Bring everyone home.

588
00:53:01,560 --> 00:53:03,080
Yes, sir.

589
00:53:12,040 --> 00:53:12,840
Thank you.

590
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:17,760
Well.

591
00:53:18,960 --> 00:53:22,400
Thank you for telling me about my dad.

592
00:53:25,480 --> 00:53:26,680
And…

593
00:53:28,480 --> 00:53:31,520
for getting Oab and me out of that place.

594
00:53:32,920 --> 00:53:34,120
Honestly,

595
00:53:34,920 --> 00:53:37,640
I've never seen this side of you before.

596
00:53:39,840 --> 00:53:41,040
Like what?

597
00:53:42,240 --> 00:53:43,440
Like…

598
00:53:44,280 --> 00:53:45,920
Well…

599
00:53:47,040 --> 00:53:48,240
your gentler side, I guess.

600
00:53:54,560 --> 00:53:55,760
And…

601
00:53:59,600 --> 00:54:01,520
thank you for protecting me too.

602
00:54:11,960 --> 00:54:13,280
Risa.

603
00:54:15,720 --> 00:54:17,000
From now on,

604
00:54:18,280 --> 00:54:20,680
I'll protect you until we find Aek.

605
00:54:24,720 --> 00:54:25,680
Promise me.

606
00:54:30,280 --> 00:54:31,400
I promise.

607
00:55:14,720 --> 00:55:15,480
Ris!

608
00:55:23,600 --> 00:55:24,560
Hey, Pao!

609
00:55:26,560 --> 00:55:28,880
Angpao, be careful. Don't fall. Hurry up.

610
00:55:28,960 --> 00:55:30,160
Koh!

611
00:55:51,480 --> 00:55:53,320
I want you to find out
what they're planning next.

612
00:55:53,400 --> 00:55:55,600
Isn't that actually good for us?

613
00:55:55,680 --> 00:55:57,320
They're helping us
take down criminals anyway.

614
00:55:57,400 --> 00:55:59,040
Catching criminals is our job.

615
00:56:00,080 --> 00:56:00,960
Not theirs.

616
00:56:01,040 --> 00:56:02,400
<i>Everyone, there's a checkpoint up ahead.</i>

617
00:56:02,480 --> 00:56:04,040
Didn't Lin say everything was cleared?

618
00:56:04,120 --> 00:56:05,920
What do we do? Just ram through it?

619
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:08,200
<i>-Are you Thai?</i>
<i>-We already cleared everything.</i>

620
00:56:08,280 --> 00:56:09,720
<i>Are you sure it was cleared?</i>

621
00:56:09,800 --> 00:56:11,240
Everyone, get down!

622
00:56:16,160 --> 00:56:18,240
<i>I've taken care of them,</i>
<i>just like you asked.</i>

623
00:56:18,320 --> 00:56:20,120
<i>Don't forget your promise.</i>

624
00:56:20,200 --> 00:56:21,600
Go back and do your job properly.

625
00:56:21,680 --> 00:56:25,200
When the time is right, I'll let you know.

626
00:56:25,280 --> 00:56:27,440
When the right moment comes,

627
00:56:27,520 --> 00:56:29,320
I'm going all in.

628
00:57:16,520 --> 00:57:21,080
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
